.TH "libnvme_sed_lock_unlock" 9 "libnvme_sed_lock_unlock" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvme_sed_lock_unlock \- Change the lock state of the global range
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvme_sed_lock_unlock
.BI "(struct libnvme_transport_handle *hdl "  ","
.BI "const struct libnvme_sed_key *key "  ","
.BI "enum libnvme_sed_lock_state state "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "hdl" 12
Transport handle
.IP "key" 12
Admin1 password
.IP "state" 12
New lock state, see \fIenum libnvme_sed_lock_state\fP
.SH "RETURN"
See the return value convention above.
